From: djsaunde <1245942+djsaunde@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:09:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] fast: OpenGL ES 3.0 backend fixes (USE_OPENGLES)

LUS's GLES path compiled but lacked what the port's N64 rendering uses. Only USE_OPENGLES builds change:
- the fragment shader is highp (float, int, sampler2D: a lowp sampler gave texels 1 level off on Mesa, and
  Adreno runs mediump / lowp at half precision);
- GL_DEPTH_CLAMP through GL_EXT_depth_clamp, else the far plane clamped in the vertex shader (near is patch 12's
  clipping); the old `gl_Position.z *= 0.3` hack is gone (it changed every depth value);
- G_TX_MIRROR | G_TX_CLAMP: GL_MIRROR_CLAMP_TO_EDGE only with GL_EXT_texture_mirror_clamp_to_edge, else
  mirrored repeat (the enum is not core ES);
- GetPixelDepth: ES reads no depth with glReadPixels. GL_NV_read_depth when present, else each pixel is blitted
  into a DEPTH24_STENCIL8 texture and drawn as a 24-bit integer into RGBA8; same values as the desktop path;
- no MSAA (ES 3.0 resolves only to the same size and format, and Fast3D resolves scaled);
- shader compile errors print the log and the source.
FAST_GLES_NO_EXT=1 (or a list: depth_clamp, mirror_clamp, read_depth) takes the fallbacks. Patch 13's
screen-linear shading needs no extension (it does not use noperspective).
